        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "The Plan provides an out-of-area emergency benefit for dental services and supplies provided by a licensed dentist who is not a member of the prepaid provider network. Out-of-area means the covered person is more than fifty (50) miles from the selected participating provider. The Plan pays reasonable charges for these services and supplies, without prior approval, to a maximum of $50. Payment for out-of-area emergencies is made only if all these conditions apply.",
